    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="1070" n="936" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg936"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    J. C. S. Files</note>
                <head>No. 615<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Representatives of the
                        British Chiefs of Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d615-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C. C. S. 889</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-06">6 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Contribution to the Final Phase of the War
                        Against Japan
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <table>
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>References:</cell>
                        <cell>CCS 452 Series</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>CCS 619 Series</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>CCS 691 Series</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>We have been instructed to present the attached memorandum on the British
                        contribution to the final phase of the war against Japan, which the British Chiefs of Staff have prepared for
                        discussion at the next conference.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The views of the Australian and New Zealand Governments on the proposals
                        formulated have been requested but have not yet been received.<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d615-f2"/>
                    </item>
                </list>


                <xi:include href="d615-a1.xml" xpointer="d615-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d615-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d615-f1-content">
                <p>Considered by the Combined Chiefs of Staff at their 194th Meeting, July 17. See
                        <ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_48">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ii</hi>, pp. 48</ref>–<ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_51"
                    >51</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d615-f2" n="2" xml:id="d615-f2-content">
                <p>For the substance of the Australian views, see Ehrman, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grand Strategy</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >vi</hi>, p. 268. The New Zealand views were not received prior to the
                    conclusion of the meetings of the Combined Chiefs of Staff held in connection
                    with the Berlin Conference. See <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 269.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
